{"task_id": "Mbpp/62", "solution": "def smallest_num(numbers: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the smallest number in a list by delegating to an internal NumberList class.\"\"\"\n    class NumberList:\n        def __init__(self, numbers: list):\n            self.numbers = numbers\n\n        def find_smallest(self) -> int:\n            if not self.numbers:\n                # Assuming non-empty lists based on design context example.\n                # If an empty list can be passed, a ValueError or similar check would be needed.\n                return None # Or raise an error\n            \n            smallest = self.numbers[0]\n            for num in self.numbers:\n                if num < smallest:\n                    smallest = num\n            return smallest\n\n    number_list_instance = NumberList(numbers)\n    return number_list_instance.find_smallest()"}
