{"task_id": "Mbpp/65", "solution": "from typing import Any, List\ndef recursive_list_sum(lst: List[Any]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Recursively flattens a nested list of integers and returns the sum of all elements.\n    The original list is left unmodified.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = 0\n    # Initialize the stack with elements of the input list in reverse order\n    # so that they are processed in their original (left-to-right) order when popped.\n    stack = list(reversed(lst))\n\n    while stack:\n        current_element = stack.pop()\n\n        if isinstance(current_element, list):\n            # If the element is a list, push its elements onto the stack in reverse order.\n            stack.extend(reversed(current_element))\n        elif isinstance(current_element, int):\n            # If the element is an integer, add it to the running sum.\n            total += current_element\n        # As per instructions, no handling for other types is included.\n\n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/66", "solution": "def pos_count(numbers):\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of positive numbers in a given list.\n    This implementation orchestrates NumberList and PositiveCounter as per the design.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class NumberList:\n        \"\"\"A simple class to hold a list of numbers.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, numbers_list):\n            self.numbers = numbers_list\n\n    class PositiveCounter:\n        \"\"\"A service class responsible for counting positive numbers.\"\"\"\n        def countPositiveNumbers(self, number_list_instance):\n            count = 0\n            for num in number_list_instance.numbers:\n                if num > 0:\n                    count += 1\n            return count\n\n    # Orchestrate the components as per the design document's System Implementation.\n    number_list_obj = NumberList(numbers)\n    counter_obj = PositiveCounter()\n    result = counter_obj.countPositiveNumbers(number_list_obj)\n    return result"}
