{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is undulating, where digits strictly alternate between increasing and decreasing.\"\"\"\n    s_number = str(number)\n    n = len(s_number)\n\n    if n < 2:\n        return True\n\n    digits = [int(char) for char in s_number]\n\n    # Check the first pair of digits to set the initial trend.\n    if digits[0] == digits[1]:\n        return False\n    \n    # If digits[0] < digits[1], the first pair increased, so we expect the next to decrease.\n    # Therefore, 'expect_increase' is True if the first pair decreased, expecting an increase next.\n    expect_increase = (digits[0] > digits[1])\n\n    for i in range(2, n):\n        if digits[i] == digits[i-1]:\n            return False\n        \n        current_is_increasing = (digits[i] > digits[i-1])\n\n        if current_is_increasing != expect_increase:\n            return False\n        \n        # Flip the expected trend for the next comparison.\n        expect_increase = not expect_increase\n            \n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/93", "solution": "def power(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Calculates 'a' to the power of 'b' using binary exponentiation.\"\"\"\n    if b == 0:\n        return 1\n    if a == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    result = 1\n    current_base = a\n    current_exponent = b\n\n    # Iterative binary exponentiation for non-negative exponents.\n    # For negative exponents, the result would typically be a float,\n    # but the design specifies \"integer result\", implying b >= 0.\n    while current_exponent > 0:\n        if current_exponent % 2 == 1:\n            result *= current_base\n        current_base *= current_base\n        current_exponent //= 2\n    return result"}
