{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "from typing import Dict, Tuple\nclass EulerianNumberService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements the recurrence for Eulerian numbers with memoization.\n    Handles base cases and recursive computation.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self._cache: Dict[Tuple[int, int], int] = {(0, 0): 1}\n\n    def _compute_recursive(self, n: int, m: int) -> int:\n        if (n, m) in self._cache:\n            return self._cache[(n, m)]\n\n        # Base cases where the Eulerian number is 0.\n        if m < 0 or m >= n:\n            result = 0\n        # Base case for a(n, 0) = 1 for n > 0.\n        elif m == 0:\n            result = 1\n        # Recurrence relation for a(n, m).\n        else:\n            a_nm1_m1 = self._compute_recursive(n - 1, m - 1)\n            a_nm1_m = self._compute_recursive(n - 1, m)\n            result = (n - m) * a_nm1_m1 + (m + 1) * a_nm1_m\n\n        self._cache[(n, m)] = result\n        return result\nclass EulerianNumberCalculator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manages the Eulerian number computation by delegating to the service.\n    This class is a thin wrapper around the service.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self._service = EulerianNumberService()\n\n    def compute(self, n: int, m: int) -> int:\n        return self._service._compute_recursive(n, m)\ndef eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m) using a memoized recursive approach.\n    It leverages internal service and calculator classes.\n    \"\"\"\n    calculator = EulerianNumberCalculator()\n    return calculator.compute(n, m)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/104", "solution": "def sort_sublists(list_of_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts each sublist of strings in a given list of lists lexicographically.\n    Returns a new list of lists with sorted sublists, without modifying the input.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_collection = []\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        sorted_sublist = sorted(sublist)\n        sorted_collection.append(sorted_sublist)\n    return sorted_collection"}
