{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of times a binary string, after being rotated, represents an odd decimal number.\n    The initial string state is not counted as one of the rotations for the purpose of the tally.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_string = binary_string\n    \n    # Perform the specified number of rotations\n    for _ in range(rotations):\n        # Rotate the string one position to the left (move first char to the end)\n        if current_string: # Ensure string is not empty to avoid index errors\n            current_string = current_string[1:] + current_string[0]\n        else:\n            # If the string is empty, rotation does not change it.\n            # No decimal value to check, so we can continue or break.\n            # Assuming non-empty string as per context.\n            continue\n        \n        # Convert the rotated binary string to a decimal integer\n        # If current_string becomes empty, int() would raise ValueError.\n        # Given context, binary_string is expected to be non-empty.\n        decimal_value = int(current_string, 2)\n        \n        # Check if the decimal value is odd\n        if decimal_value % 2 != 0:\n            odd_count += 1\n            \n    return odd_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "def common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the common elements across all inner lists in a nested list.\n    Returns a set of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    # Convert the first inner list to a set to start the intersection\n    common_elements = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    # Iterate through the remaining inner lists and compute the intersection\n    for inner_list in nested_lists[1:]:\n        common_elements.intersection_update(set(inner_list))\n\n    return common_elements"}
