{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(binaryString: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the maximum absolute difference between the number of 0s and 1s\n    in any contiguous substring of the input binary string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not binaryString:\n        return 0\n\n    # Validate input and transform '0' to 1, '1' to -1.\n    # The problem reduces to finding the maximum subarray sum.\n    transformed_values = []\n    for ch in binaryString:\n        if ch == '0':\n            transformed_values.append(1)\n        elif ch == '1':\n            transformed_values.append(-1)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid character '{ch}' in binary string.\")\n\n    current_max = 0\n    global_max = 0\n\n    # Apply Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum subarray sum.\n    for val in transformed_values:\n        current_max = max(val, current_max + val)\n        global_max = max(global_max, current_max)\n\n    return global_max"}
