{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(array: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the ratio of zero elements to non-zero elements in an integer array.\n    Handles empty arrays and cases with no non-zero elements by returning 0.0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return 0.0\n\n    zero_count = 0\n    non_zero_count = 0\n\n    for x in array:\n        if x == 0:\n            zero_count += 1\n        else:\n            non_zero_count += 1\n\n    if non_zero_count == 0:\n        return 0.0\n\n    return zero_count / non_zero_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number can be represented as a sum of distinct non-zero powers of two.\n    This means the number must be positive and even, as 2^0 is excluded.\n    \"\"\"\n    # A number can be represented as a sum of distinct non-zero powers of two\n    # if and only if its binary representation contains only '1' bits at positions\n    # corresponding to exponents greater than or equal to 1.\n    # This implies the number must be even (as the 2^0 bit must be 0)\n    # and greater than 0 (as 0 is not a sum of powers of two).\n    # Since 1 corresponds to 2^0, it cannot be represented.\n    # Thus, the number must be at least 2 and even.\n    return number >= 2 and number % 2 == 0"}
