{"task_id": "Mbpp/167", "solution": "def next_power_of_2(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the smallest power of two greater than or equal to `n`.\n    Uses bitwise operations for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 1\n\n    n -= 1\n    n |= n >> 1\n    n |= n >> 2\n    n |= n >> 4\n    n |= n >> 8\n    n |= n >> 16\n    # For 64-bit integers, n |= n >> 32 might be needed for larger inputs, but Python handles arbitrary precision.\n    return n + 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "def sum_range_list(lst: list[int], startIndex: int, endIndex: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the arithmetic sum of a contiguous subsequence of a list of integers within specified inclusive indices.\n    Raises `ValueError` for invalid indices or range, returns 0 for an empty list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return 0\n\n    if startIndex > endIndex:\n        raise ValueError(\"startIndex must be <= endIndex\")\n\n    if startIndex < 0 or endIndex >= len(lst):\n        raise ValueError(\"Indices out of bounds\")\n\n    return sum(lst[startIndex:endIndex + 1])"}
