{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even bits of the input integer to 1.\n    This implementation uses a fixed mask 0x55555555 (01010101... in binary)\n    which sets even-indexed bits (0, 2, 4, ... from right) to 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The mask 0x55555555 has all even bits set to 1 and odd bits set to 0.\n    # For a 32-bit number, this is 01010101 01010101 01010101 01010101.\n    # Using a bitwise OR operation with this mask will set all even bits of 'n' to 1\n    # while preserving the odd bits of 'n'.\n    EVEN_BITS_MASK = 0x55555555\n    return n | EVEN_BITS_MASK"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(list_of_tuples: list[tuple]) -> dict[tuple, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the occurrences of each unique tuple in a list,\n    canonicalizing tuples by sorting their elements before counting.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for original_tuple in list_of_tuples:\n        # Sort elements within the tuple to create a canonical key\n        canonical_key = tuple(sorted(original_tuple))\n        counts[canonical_key] = counts.get(canonical_key, 0) + 1\n    return counts"}
