{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    # dp_prev stores the counts of sequences of length (current_length - 1) ending at each value.\n    # Initialize for length 1: any value from 1 to m is a valid sequence.\n    dp_prev = [0] * (m + 1)\n    for x in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp_prev[x] = 1\n\n    # Iterate for lengths from 2 up to n, updating counts based on the previous length.\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        dp_curr = [0] * (m + 1)\n        # Calculate prefix sums for dp_prev to efficiently find the sum of counts for previous elements.\n        prefix_sum_dp_prev = [0] * (m + 1)\n        for x_val in range(1, m + 1):\n            prefix_sum_dp_prev[x_val] = prefix_sum_dp_prev[x_val - 1] + dp_prev[x_val]\n\n        # Calculate dp_curr based on prefix sums of dp_prev.\n        for x_val in range(1, m + 1):\n            # A sequence of length 'length' ending in x_val requires its previous element 'prev_val'\n            # to satisfy prev_val * 2 <= x_val, which means prev_val <= x_val // 2.\n            # The count is the sum of all sequences of length (length - 1) ending in any such 'prev_val'.\n            dp_curr[x_val] = prefix_sum_dp_prev[x_val // 2]\n        \n        dp_prev = dp_curr\n\n    # The total number of sequences of length n is the sum of all elements in dp_prev.\n    return sum(dp_prev)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # lis_sum[i] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at array[i].\n    lis_sum = list(array)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if array[j] < array[i]:\n                lis_sum[i] = max(lis_sum[i], lis_sum[j] + array[i])\n\n    # lds_sum[i] stores the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at array[i].\n    lds_sum = list(array)\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if array[j] < array[i]:\n                lds_sum[i] = max(lds_sum[i], lds_sum[j] + array[i])\n\n    max_overall_sum = float('-inf')\n\n    # A bitonic subsequence peaks at some element array[i].\n    # Its total sum is (sum of LIS ending at i) + (sum of LDS starting at i) - array[i]\n    # (as array[i] is counted twice).\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sum[i] + lds_sum[i] - array[i]\n        max_overall_sum = max(max_overall_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_overall_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence using dynamic programming.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the LPS for the substring s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for substring lengths from 2 to n\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                if length == 2:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2\n                else:\n                    dp[i][j] = dp[i + 1][j - 1] + 2\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
