{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(num):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers less than the given non-negative number.\n    Raises ValueError if the input is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input number must be non-negative.\")\n\n    if num <= 2:\n        return 0\n\n    prime_count = 0\n    # Iterate through numbers from 2 up to num-1\n    for i in range(2, num):\n        is_current_num_prime = True\n        if i <= 1:  # Numbers less than or equal to 1 are not prime\n            is_current_num_prime = False\n        elif i == 2:  # 2 is the only even prime number\n            is_current_num_prime = True\n        elif i % 2 == 0:  # All other even numbers are not prime\n            is_current_num_prime = False\n        else:\n            # Check for odd divisors from 3 up to the square root of i\n            # We increment by 2 because we only need to check odd divisors\n            limit = int(i**0.5) + 1\n            for divisor in range(3, limit, 2):\n                if i % divisor == 0:\n                    is_current_num_prime = False\n                    break\n        \n        if is_current_num_prime:\n            prime_count += 1\n            \n    return prime_count"}
