{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "from collections import deque\ndef kadane_with_length_constraint_optimized(arr, max_len):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum subarray sum in 'arr' with a maximum length constraint 'max_len'.\n    Uses prefix sums and a deque for efficient O(N) calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n    \n    n_arr = len(arr)\n    \n    # Initialize max_so_far with the largest single element to handle all-negative arrays.\n    max_so_far = max(arr)\n    \n    # If max_len is 1, the result is simply the max single element.\n    if max_len == 1:\n        return max_so_far\n\n    prefix_sums = [0] * (n_arr + 1)\n    for i in range(n_arr):\n        prefix_sums[i+1] = prefix_sums[i] + arr[i]\n    \n    dq = deque()\n    dq.append(0) # Store index 0 for prefix_sums[0] = 0\n    \n    for j in range(1, n_arr + 1):\n        # Remove indices from the left that violate the max_len constraint.\n        # A subarray from index `i` to `j-1` has length `j - i`. We need `j - i <= max_len`.\n        while dq and dq[0] < j - max_len:\n            dq.popleft()\n        \n        # Calculate max subarray sum ending at `j-1` using `prefix_sums[j] - prefix_sums[dq[0]]`.\n        if dq:\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, prefix_sums[j] - prefix_sums[dq[0]])\n        \n        # Maintain monotonic increasing deque for prefix sums.\n        while dq and prefix_sums[dq[-1]] >= prefix_sums[j]:\n            dq.pop()\n        dq.append(j)\n            \n    return max_so_far\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr, k, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous array in the modified array formed by repeating\n    the given array k times, with a maximum subarray length n.\n    \"\"\"\n    L = len(arr)\n    if L == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    total_sum_arr = sum(arr)\n    \n    # Calculate max prefix sum for a single block of arr (must be non-empty).\n    max_prefix_val = float('-inf')\n    current_prefix_sum = 0\n    for val in arr:\n        current_prefix_sum += val\n        max_prefix_val = max(max_prefix_val, current_prefix_sum)\n    \n    # Calculate max suffix sum for a single block of arr (must be non-empty).\n    max_suffix_val = float('-inf')\n    current_suffix_sum = 0\n    for i in range(L - 1, -1, -1):\n        current_suffix_sum += arr[i]\n        max_suffix_val = max(max_suffix_val, current_suffix_sum)\n\n    # Base case: maximum sum within one or two concatenations, respecting 'n'.\n    # We use min(k, 2) repetitions as the effective array for base calculation.\n    effective_arr_length = min(k, 2) * L\n    arr_for_base = arr * min(k, 2)\n    res = kadane_with_length_constraint_optimized(arr_for_base, n)\n\n    # If k is greater than 2 and the total sum of array is positive,\n    # consider sums formed by (k-2) full repetitions plus max prefix/suffix parts.\n    if k > 2 and total_sum_arr > 0:\n        # This formula captures the maximum sum if n is large enough to span multiple blocks.\n        # It takes the max suffix from the first block, (k-2) full blocks, and max prefix from the last block.\n        res = max(res, max_prefix_val + (k - 2) * total_sum_arr + max_suffix_val)\n    \n    return res"}
