{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "def get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum sum using the recurrence f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    Uses memoization to optimize performance for repeated calculations.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Using a dictionary for memoization. This cache will persist across calls\n    # within the same interpreter session.\n    # Alternatively, functools.lru_cache could be used if allowed to modify the decorator.\n    # For a standalone function that needs a cache, a closure or a mutable default argument\n    # are common patterns if decorators are not desired/allowed for specific reasons.\n    # Given the prompt, a simple dict within a closure or using a global/module-level dict is implied\n    # if lru_cache isn't explicitly shown.\n    # Let's use a dictionary defined inside the function if it's supposed to be self-contained\n    # or a module-level cache if it's meant to be persistent.\n    # The design context shows `_cache = {}` inside a class, so for a standalone function,\n    # a module-level cache (like `lru_cache` provides or a global dict) is appropriate for persistence.\n\n    # To adhere strictly to \"No class wrapper\" and make it self-contained for the stub,\n    # but still use memoization, a dictionary as a function attribute can simulate persistence\n    # across calls to the same function object, or a global/module-level dict.\n    # lru_cache is the standard Pythonic way for recursive function memoization.\n\n    # Re-evaluating the \"No class wrapper\" and the design context showing `lru_cache`\n    # in the comments of the provided implementation snippet:\n    # `from functools import lru_cache`\n    # This strongly suggests `lru_cache` is the intended mechanism for memoization\n    # for a standalone function.\n\n    from functools import lru_cache\n\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None) # maxsize=None means cache grows without limit\n    def _memoized_get_max_sum(current_n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Helper function with memoization.\"\"\"\n        if current_n <= 0:\n            return current_n\n\n        # Recursive calls with integer division\n        sum_parts = (\n            _memoized_get_max_sum(current_n // 2) +\n            _memoized_get_max_sum(current_n // 3) +\n            _memoized_get_max_sum(current_n // 4) +\n            _memoized_get_max_sum(current_n // 5)\n        )\n\n        return max(sum_parts, current_n)\n\n    return _memoized_get_max_sum(n)"}
