{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "class IntegerPair:\n    \"\"\"Represents a pair of integers and calculates their product.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, first: int, second: int):\n        self.first = first\n        self.second = second\n\n    def product(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the product of the two integers.\"\"\"\n        return self.first * self.second\nclass ProductList:\n    \"\"\"Manages a list of IntegerPair objects and finds their minimum product.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, integer_pairs: list[IntegerPair]):\n        self.pairs = integer_pairs\n\n    def min_product(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates and returns the minimum product among all pairs.\"\"\"\n        products = [pair.product() for pair in self.pairs]\n        return min(products)\ndef min_product_tuple(pairs: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum product from the pairs of tuples within a given list.\n    This function orchestrates domain logic to calculate the minimum product.\n    \"\"\"\n    integer_pair_objects = [IntegerPair(t[0], t[1]) for t in pairs]\n    product_list_instance = ProductList(integer_pair_objects)\n    return product_list_instance.min_product()"}
