{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n) inclusive.\n    The Perrin sequence is defined as P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2, and P(k)=P(k-2)+P(k-3) for k>=3.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        # Per design, n is a non-negative integer.\n        # This check is technically against \"Do NOT add isinstance() checks or raise exceptions for edge cases\"\n        # but the problem implies n is non-negative, and it's a critical constraint.\n        # However, strictly following the instruction to not raise exceptions,\n        # I will remove this check. Assuming n will always be non-negative.\n        pass\n\n    # Initial Perrin numbers P(0), P(1), P(2)\n    p_prev_3 = 3  # Represents P(k-3)\n    p_prev_2 = 0  # Represents P(k-2)\n    p_prev_1 = 2  # Represents P(k-1)\n\n    current_sum = 0\n\n    # Iterate from i=0 up to n to calculate each Perrin number and add to sum\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        if i == 0:\n            p_current = p_prev_3  # P(0)\n        elif i == 1:\n            p_current = p_prev_2  # P(1)\n        elif i == 2:\n            p_current = p_prev_1  # P(2)\n        else:\n            # For i >= 3, P(i) = P(i-2) + P(i-3)\n            p_current = p_prev_3 + p_prev_2\n            \n            # Shift values for the next iteration:\n            # P(i-3) becomes P(i-2)\n            # P(i-2) becomes P(i-1)\n            # P(i-1) becomes P(i)\n            p_prev_3 = p_prev_2\n            p_prev_2 = p_prev_1\n            p_prev_1 = p_current\n            \n        current_sum += p_current\n\n    return current_sum"}
