{"task_id": "Mbpp/478", "solution": "def remove_lowercase(input: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Remove all contiguous ASCII lowercase letter substrings from the input string.\n    The order of remaining characters is preserved.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    i = 0\n    n = len(input)\n\n    while i < n:\n        # Check if the current character is an ASCII lowercase letter\n        if 'a' <= input[i] <= 'z':\n            # If it is, skip all subsequent contiguous lowercase letters\n            while i < n and 'a' <= input[i] <= 'z':\n                i += 1\n            # After skipping, continue to the next character in the outer loop\n            continue\n        else:\n            # If it's not a lowercase letter, append it to the result\n            result.append(input[i])\n            i += 1\n            \n    return ''.join(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/479", "solution": "def first_Digit(number):\n    \"\"\"Finds the first digit of a given number.\"\"\"\n    abs_num = abs(number)\n    if abs_num == 0:\n        return 0\n    while abs_num >= 10:\n        abs_num //= 10\n    return abs_num"}
