{"task_id": "Mbpp/583", "solution": "def catalan_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Catalan number using the closed-form formula.\n    C(n) = (1/(n+1)) * C(2n, n)\n    \"\"\"\n\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Catalan number is not defined for negative input.\")\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Helper function to calculate binomial coefficient C(N, K)\n    def binomial_coefficient(N, K):\n        if K < 0 or K > N:\n            return 0\n        if K == 0 or K == N:\n            return 1\n        if K > N // 2:\n            K = N - K\n        \n        res = 1\n        for i in range(K):\n            res = res * (N - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    # Calculate C(2n, n)\n    binomial_2n_n = binomial_coefficient(2 * n, n)\n\n    # Apply the formula C(n) = C(2n, n) / (n + 1)\n    return binomial_2n_n // (n + 1)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/586", "solution": "def split_Arr(list_to_split, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list at the nth element and adds the first part to the end.\n    Handles edge cases for n out of bounds by returning the original list.\n    \"\"\"\n    length = len(list_to_split)\n    if n <= 0 or n >= length:\n        return list_to_split[:] # Return a shallow copy if n is out of bounds\n\n    first_part = list_to_split[:n]\n    second_part = list_to_split[n:]\n\n    return second_part + first_part"}
