{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import List\ndef perfect_squares(lower: int, upper: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return all perfect squares between lower and upper inclusive.\"\"\"\n    start = math.isqrt(lower)\n    # If the square of 'start' is less than 'lower', it means 'lower' itself\n    # is not a perfect square, and 'start' is the floor of its square root.\n    # We need to increment 'start' to find the next integer whose square\n    # might be within the range.\n    if start * start < lower:\n        start += 1\n    \n    end = math.isqrt(upper)\n\n    squares = []\n    for n in range(start, end + 1):\n        squares.append(n * n)\n    return squares"}
