{"task_id": "Mbpp/594", "solution": "def diff_even_odd(numbers: List[int]) -> Optional[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the difference between the first even and first odd number in a list.\n    Raises ValueError if the list is empty, or if an even or odd number is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class NumberList:\n        \"\"\"Helper class to encapsulate operations on a list of numbers.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, numbers: List[int]):\n            self.numbers = numbers\n\n        def get_first_even(self) -> Optional[int]:\n            \"\"\"Returns the first even number in the list, or None if not found.\"\"\"\n            for num in self.numbers:\n                if num % 2 == 0:\n                    return num\n            return None\n\n        def get_first_odd(self) -> Optional[int]:\n            \"\"\"Returns the first odd number in the list, or None if not found.\"\"\"\n            for num in self.numbers:\n                if num % 2 != 0:\n                    return num\n            return None\n\n    if not numbers:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list is empty.\")\n\n    num_list_obj = NumberList(numbers)\n    first_even = num_list_obj.get_first_even()\n    first_odd = num_list_obj.get_first_odd()\n\n    if first_even is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"No even number found.\")\n    if first_odd is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"No odd number found.\")\n\n    return first_even - first_odd"}
