{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "def find_kth(array1, array2, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the k-th smallest element from two sorted arrays using a binary search approach.\n    Assumes k is 1-indexed and inputs are valid sorted arrays.\n    \"\"\"\n    m, n = len(array1), len(array2)\n\n    # Ensure array1 is the smaller array to optimize binary search range.\n    if m > n:\n        array1, array2 = array2, array1\n        m, n = n, m\n\n    # Binary search for the split point 'i' in array1.\n    # 'i' represents the number of elements taken from array1 for the left partition.\n    # 'j = k - i' represents the number of elements taken from array2 for the left partition.\n    low = max(0, k - n)\n    high = min(k, m)\n\n    while low <= high:\n        i = (low + high) // 2\n        j = k - i\n\n        # Determine the elements at the partition boundaries.\n        # Use negative/positive infinity for boundary conditions (i=0, j=0, i=m, j=n).\n        left_part1_max = array1[i-1] if i > 0 else -float('inf')\n        left_part2_max = array2[j-1] if j > 0 else -float('inf')\n        right_part1_min = array1[i] if i < m else float('inf')\n        right_part2_min = array2[j] if j < n else float('inf')\n\n        # Check if the partition is correct: left_max elements <= right_min elements.\n        if left_part1_max <= right_part2_min and left_part2_max <= right_part1_min:\n            return max(left_part1_max, left_part2_max)\n        elif left_part1_max > right_part2_min:\n            # Too many elements taken from array1, need to shift 'i' left.\n            high = i - 1\n        else: # left_part2_max > right_part1_min\n            # Too few elements taken from array1, need to shift 'i' right.\n            low = i + 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/602", "solution": "from typing import Optional, Set\nclass InputString:\n    \"\"\"Immutable value object representing the input string.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: str):\n        self.value = value\nclass RepeatedCharacter:\n    \"\"\"Immutable value object representing the repeated character.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: Optional[str]):\n        self.value = value\nclass FindFirstRepeatedChar:\n    \"\"\"Service that finds the first repeated character.\"\"\"\n    def execute(self, input_obj: InputString) -> RepeatedCharacter:\n        seen: Set[str] = set()\n        for ch in input_obj.value:\n            if ch in seen:\n                return RepeatedCharacter(ch)\n            seen.add(ch)\n        return RepeatedCharacter(None)\ndef first_repeated_char(input_string: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the first repeated character in *input_string*.\n    If no character repeats, return None.\n    \"\"\"\n    domain_input = InputString(input_string)\n    service = FindFirstRepeatedChar()\n    result = service.execute(domain_input)\n    return result.value"}
