{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using the Bell triangle algorithm.\n    The Bell triangle iteratively computes Bell numbers from previous values.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize the Bell triangle. triangle[i] stores the i-th row.\n    # Each row i will have i+1 elements.\n    triangle = []\n    triangle.append([1]) # B(0) = 1 is the first element of the 0-th row\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        current_row = [0] * (i + 1)\n        \n        # The first element of the current row is the last element of the previous row.\n        current_row[0] = triangle[i-1][-1]\n\n        # Fill the rest of the current row using the sum of the element to its left\n        # and the element diagonally above-left from the previous row.\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            current_row[j] = current_row[j-1] + triangle[i-1][j-1]\n        \n        triangle.append(current_row)\n    \n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row of the triangle.\n    return triangle[n][0]"}
