{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of integers using the heap sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list, preserving the original input_list.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr = list(input_list)  # Create a copy to not modify the original list\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Helper function to maintain the max-heap property\n    def heapify(arr_local, n_local, i_local):\n        largest = i_local\n        left = 2 * i_local + 1\n        right = 2 * i_local + 2\n\n        if left < n_local and arr_local[left] > arr_local[largest]:\n            largest = left\n\n        if right < n_local and arr_local[right] > arr_local[largest]:\n            largest = right\n\n        if largest != i_local:\n            arr_local[i_local], arr_local[largest] = arr_local[largest], arr_local[i_local]\n            heapify(arr_local, n_local, largest)\n\n    # Build a maxheap\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n    # Extract elements one by one from the heap\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]  # Move current root to end\n        heapify(arr, i, 0)  # Call max heapify on the reduced heap\n\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "import math\ndef wind_chill(wind_velocity_kmh: float, temperature_c: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index given wind velocity in km/h and temperature in Celsius.\n    The result is rounded to the nearest integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Standard meteorological wind chill formula (Canadian/US NWS standard for C and km/h)\n    # Twc = 13.12 + 0.6215Ta - 11.37V^0.16 + 0.3965TaV^0.16\n    # Where Ta is air temperature in Celsius, and V is wind velocity in km/h.\n\n    # Calculate the raw wind chill index using the formula.\n    wind_chill_index_raw = (\n        13.12\n        + (0.6215 * temperature_c)\n        - (11.37 * (wind_velocity_kmh**0.16))\n        + (0.3965 * temperature_c * (wind_velocity_kmh**0.16))\n    )\n\n    # Round the result to the nearest integer as indicated by the example and \"next integer\" phrasing.\n    rounded_index = round(wind_chill_index_raw)\n\n    return int(rounded_index)"}
