{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum average cost of a path from the top-left to the bottom-right cell\n    in a square matrix, moving only right or down.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(matrix)\n    \n    # dp_sum[r][c] stores the maximum sum of costs to reach cell (r, c)\n    dp_sum = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Base case: top-left cell\n    dp_sum[0][0] = matrix[0][0]\n\n    # Fill the first row\n    for c in range(1, n):\n        dp_sum[0][c] = matrix[0][c] + dp_sum[0][c - 1]\n\n    # Fill the first column\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        dp_sum[r][0] = matrix[r][0] + dp_sum[r - 1][0]\n\n    # Fill the rest of the DP table\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        for c in range(1, n):\n            dp_sum[r][c] = matrix[r][c] + max(dp_sum[r - 1][c], dp_sum[r][c - 1])\n\n    # The number of cells in any path from (0,0) to (n-1, n-1) is always (n-1) + (n-1) + 1\n    num_cells_in_path = (n - 1) + (n - 1) + 1 \n    \n    # Calculate the maximum average\n    max_total_cost = dp_sum[n - 1][n - 1]\n    return max_total_cost / num_cells_in_path"}
