{"task_id": "Mbpp/724", "solution": "def power_base_sum(base: int, power: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all digits of the base to the specified power.\n    e.g., power_base_sum(2, 100) == 115\n    \"\"\"\n    class PowerCalculator:\n        \"\"\"Helper class to calculate base^power and sum its digits.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, base_val: int, power_val: int):\n            self.base = base_val\n            self.power = power_val\n\n        def sum_digits(self) -> int:\n            \"\"\"Calculates base^power and returns the sum of its decimal digits.\"\"\"\n            result = self.base ** self.power\n            digit_sum = 0\n            # Convert the number to a string and iterate through its characters to sum digits\n            for digit_char in str(result):\n                digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n            return digit_sum\n\n    # Instantiate PowerCalculator and call its sum_digits method as per design\n    calculator = PowerCalculator(base, power)\n    return calculator.sum_digits()"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/725", "solution": "def extract_quotation(text):\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts values between double quotation marks from the given string.\n    Processes the string character by character to find quoted segments.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    in_quote = False\n    current_quote_start = -1\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(text):\n        if char == '\"':\n            if in_quote:\n                # End of a quoted segment, extract it\n                results.append(text[current_quote_start:i])\n                in_quote = False\n            else:\n                # Start of a quoted segment\n                in_quote = True\n                current_quote_start = i + 1\n    return results"}
