{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit unsigned integer left by d bits.\n    \"\"\"\n    BIT_WIDTH = 32\n    MASK = (1 << BIT_WIDTH) - 1\n\n    # Normalize the shift amount\n    d = d % BIT_WIDTH\n\n    # Perform the left rotation\n    # The first part shifts bits left, potentially exceeding 32 bits\n    # The second part shifts the overflowed bits back to the right end\n    # The result is then masked to ensure it remains a 32-bit unsigned integer\n    rotated_number = ((number << d) | (number >> (BIT_WIDTH - d))) & MASK\n    return rotated_number"}
